---
description: Unit testing conventions
alwaysApply: true
---

Unit test rules:
- Every test must contain a short description comment/docstring explaining the expected behavior.
- Use Arrange / Act / Assert structure in every test.
- Keep each section explicitly labeled.
- Tests should verify one behavior only.
- Prefer small deterministic tests.
- Test names should clearly describe expected behavior.

Example:

def test_has_module_upstream_detects_previous_module():
    """
    _has_module_upstream should return True when a module exists before the node.
    """

    # Arrange
    model = ModelFactory.simple_chain_3()
    gm = fx.symbolic_trace(model)
    l2_node = next(
        n for n in gm.graph.nodes
        if n.op == "call_module" and n.target == "l2"
    )

    # Act
    result = _has_module_upstream(l2_node)

    # Assert
    assert result is True